  <section class=3D"tex2jax_ignore mathjax_ignore" id=3D"support-for-contai=
ner-device-interface">
<span id=3D"cdi-support"></span><h1>Support for Container Device Interface<=
a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-nat=
ive/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#support-for-container-device-=
interface" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h1>
<section id=3D"about-the-container-device-interface">
<h2>About the Container Device Interface<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"htt=
ps://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-s=
upport.html#about-the-container-device-interface" title=3D"Permalink to thi=
s headline">#</a></h2>
<p>As of the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pr=
e">v1.12.0</span></code> release, the NVIDIA Container Toolkit includes sup=
port for generating Container Device Interface (CDI) specifications.</p>
<p>CDI is an open specification for container runtimes that abstracts what =
<em>access</em> to a device, such as an NVIDIA GPU, means, and standardizes=
 access across container runtimes.
Popular container runtimes can read and process the specification to ensure=
 that a device is available in a container.
CDI simplifies adding support for devices such as NVIDIA GPUs because the s=
pecification is applicable to all container runtimes that support CDI.</p>
<p>CDI also improves the compatibility of the NVIDIA container stack with c=
ertain features such as rootless containers.</p>
</section>
<section id=3D"generating-a-cdi-specification">
<h2>Generating a CDI Specification<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://d=
ocs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support=
.html#generating-a-cdi-specification" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">=
#</a></h2>
<section id=3D"prerequisites">
<h3>Prerequisites<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/da=
tacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#prerequisit=
es" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h3>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p>You installed either the NVIDIA Container Toolkit or you installed t=
he <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-=
container-toolkit-base</span></code> package.
The base package includes the container runtime and the <code class=3D"docu=
tils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-ctk</span></code> comm=
and-line interface, but avoids
installing the container runtime hook and transitive dependencies.
The hook and dependencies are not needed on machines that use CDI exclusive=
ly.</p></li>
<li><p>You installed an NVIDIA GPU Driver.</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id=3D"automatic-cdi-specification-generation">
<span id=3D"id1"></span><h3>Automatic CDI Specification Generation<a class=
=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/con=
tainer-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#automatic-cdi-specification-generati=
on" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h3>
<p>As of NVIDIA Container Toolkit <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">v1.18.0</span></code>, the CDI specification is aut=
omatically generated and updated by a systemd service called <code class=3D=
"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi-refresh</span=
></code>. This service:</p>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p>Automatically generates the CDI specification at <code class=3D"docu=
tils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">/var/run/cdi/nvidia.yaml</spa=
n></code> when:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The NVIDIA Container Toolkit is installed or upgraded</p></li>
<li><p>The NVIDIA GPU drivers are installed or upgraded</p></li>
<li><p>The system is rebooted</p></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>This ensures that the CDI specifications are up to date for the current =
driver
and device configuration and that CDI Devices defined in these specificatio=
ns are
available when using native CDI support in container engines such as Docker=
 or Podman.</p>
<p>Run the following command to list the available CDI Devices:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell0" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"go">nvidia-ctk=
 cdi list</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell0">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<section id=3D"known-limitations">
<h4>Known Limitations<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.co=
m/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#known-l=
imitations" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h4>
<p>The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvi=
dia-cdi-refresh</span></code> service does not currently handle the followi=
ng situations:</p>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p>The removal of NVIDIA GPU drivers</p></li>
<li><p>The reconfiguration of MIG devices</p></li>
</ul>
<p>For these scenarios, the regeneration of CDI specifications must be <a c=
lass=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/clou=
d-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#manual-cdi-specification=
-generation"><span class=3D"std std-doc">manually triggered</span></a>.</p>
</section>
<section id=3D"customizing-the-automatic-cdi-refresh-service">
<h4>Customizing the Automatic CDI Refresh Service<a class=3D"headerlink" hr=
ef=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/lat=
est/cdi-support.html#customizing-the-automatic-cdi-refresh-service" title=
=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h4>
<p>To customize the behavior of the <code class=3D"docutils literal notrans=
late"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi-refresh</span></code> service, add
environment variables to <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span=
 class=3D"pre">/etc/nvidia-container-toolkit/nvidia-cdi-refresh.env</span><=
/code>. These
variables affect the behavior of the <code class=3D"docutils literal notran=
slate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-ctk</span> <span class=3D"pre">cdi</span>=
 <span class=3D"pre">generate</span></code> command.</p>
<p>For example, to enable debug logging, update the configuration file
as follows:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell1" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1"># /etc/nvidi=
a-container-toolkit/nvidia-cdi-refresh.env</span>
<span class=3D"nv">NVIDIA_CTK_DEBUG</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span=
 class=3D"m">1</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell1">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>For a complete list of available environment variables, run <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-ctk</span> <sp=
an class=3D"pre">cdi</span> <span class=3D"pre">generate</span> <span class=
=3D"pre">--help</span></code> to view the command=E2=80=99s documentation.<=
/p>
<div class=3D"admonition important">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Important</p>
<p>Modifications to the environment file require a systemd reload and resta=
rting the
service to take effect</p>
</div>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell2" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl daemon-reload
<span class=3D"gp">$ </span>sudo systemctl restart nvidia-cdi-refresh.servi=
ce
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell2">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"managing-the-cdi-refresh-service">
<h4>Managing the CDI Refresh Service<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https:/=
/docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-suppo=
rt.html#managing-the-cdi-refresh-service" title=3D"Permalink to this headli=
ne">#</a></h4>
<p>The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvi=
dia-cdi-refresh</span></code> service consists of two systemd units:</p>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvi=
dia-cdi-refresh.path</span></code>: Monitors for changes to the system and =
triggers the service.</p></li>
<li><p><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvi=
dia-cdi-refresh.service</span></code>: Generates the CDI specifications for=
 all available devices based on
the default configuration and any overrides in the environment file.</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<p>These services can be managed using standard systemd commands.</p>
<p>When working as expected, the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslat=
e"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi-refresh.path</span></code> service is ena=
bled and active, and the
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi=
-refresh.service</span></code> is enabled and has run at least once. For ex=
ample:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell3" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl status nvidia-cdi-refresh.path
<span class=3D"go">=E2=97=8F nvidia-cdi-refresh.path - Trigger CDI refresh =
on NVIDIA driver install / uninstall events</span>
<span class=3D"go">     Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/nvidia-cdi-refr=
esh.path; enabled; preset: enabled)</span>
<span class=3D"go">     Active: active (waiting) since Fri 2025-06-27 06:04=
:54 EDT; 1h 47min ago</span>
<span class=3D"go">   Triggers: =E2=97=8F nvidia-cdi-refresh.service</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell3">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell4" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl status nvidia-cdi-refresh.service
<span class=3D"go">=E2=97=8B nvidia-cdi-refresh.service - Refresh NVIDIA CD=
I specification file</span>
<span class=3D"go">     Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/nvidia-cdi-refr=
esh.service; enabled; preset: enabled)</span>
<span class=3D"go">     Active: inactive (dead) since Fri 2025-06-27 07:17:=
26 EDT; 34min ago</span>
<span class=3D"go">TriggeredBy: =E2=97=8F nvidia-cdi-refresh.path</span>
<span class=3D"go">    Process: 1317511 ExecStart=3D/usr/bin/nvidia-ctk cdi=
 generate --output=3D/var/run/cdi/nvidia.yaml (code=3Dexited, status=3D0/SU=
CCESS)</span>
<span class=3D"go">   Main PID: 1317511 (code=3Dexited, status=3D0/SUCCESS)=
</span>
<span class=3D"go">        CPU: 562ms</span>
<span class=3D"go">...</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell4">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>If these are not enabled as expected, enable them by running:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell5" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl <span class=3D"nb">enable</span> --now nvidia-cdi-refresh.pat=
h
<span class=3D"gp">$ </span>sudo systemctl <span class=3D"nb">enable</span>=
 --now nvidia-cdi-refresh.service
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell5">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"troubleshooting-cdi-specification-generation-and-resolution"=
>
<h4>Troubleshooting CDI Specification Generation and Resolution<a class=3D"=
headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/contain=
er-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#troubleshooting-cdi-specification-genera=
tion-and-resolution" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h4>
<p>If CDI specifications for available devices are not generated or updated=
 as expected,
check the logs for the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span c=
lass=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi-refresh.service</span></code> by running:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell6" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo journalctl -u nvidia-cdi-refresh.service
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell6">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>In most cases, restarting the service should be sufficient to trigger th=
e (re)generation
of CDI specifications:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell7" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl restart nvidia-cdi-refresh.service
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell7">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>Running:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell8" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>n=
vidia-ctk --debug cdi list
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell8">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>Shows a list of available CDI Devices and any errors that occurred when =
loading CDI
Specifications from <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">/etc/cdi</span></code> or <code class=3D"docutils literal notrans=
late"><span class=3D"pre">/var/run/cdi</span></code>.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"manual-cdi-specification-generation">
<h3>Manual CDI Specification Generation<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"http=
s://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-su=
pport.html#manual-cdi-specification-generation" title=3D"Permalink to this =
headline">#</a></h3>
<p>As of the NVIDIA Container Toolkit <code class=3D"docutils literal notra=
nslate"><span class=3D"pre">v1.18.0</span></code>, the recommended mechanis=
m to regenerate CDI specifications is to restart the <code class=3D"docutil=
s literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-cdi-refresh.service</span=
></code>:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell9" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>s=
udo systemctl restart nvidia-cdi-refresh.service
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell9">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>If this does not work, or you need more flexibility, use the <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-ctk</span> <sp=
an class=3D"pre">cdi</span> <span class=3D"pre">generate</span></code> comm=
and
directly:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell10" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
sudo nvidia-ctk cdi generate --output<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>/var/run/c=
di/nvidia.yaml
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell10">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"jit-cdi-mode">
<h2>JIT-CDI Mode<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/dat=
acenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#jit-cdi-mode=
" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h2>
<p>Just-in-time CDI (JIT-CDI) mode generates an in-memory CDI specification=
 for the
NVIDIA devices that a container requests. The NVIDIA Container Runtime uses=
 this
specification to update the container configuration. JIT-CDI mode does not =
write
a persistent specification to <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">/var/run/cdi</span></code> or <code class=3D"docutils l=
iteral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">/etc/cdi</span></code>.</p>
<p>When <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nv=
idia-container-runtime.mode</span></code> is set to <code class=3D"docutils=
 literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">auto</span></code>, the runtime s=
elects JIT-CDI
mode on systems that use the NVIDIA Management Library (NVML) or Windows
Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2). Native CDI-enabled runtimes still use the
persistent specifications described in
<a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/=
cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#id1"><span class=3D"=
std std-doc">Automatic CDI Specification Generation</span></a>.</p>
<section id=3D"disabling-hooks-in-jit-cdi-mode">
<h3>Disabling Hooks in JIT-CDI Mode<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://=
docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-suppor=
t.html#disabling-hooks-in-jit-cdi-mode" title=3D"Permalink to this headline=
">#</a></h3>
<p>You can prevent JIT-CDI mode from adding specific hooks to an in-memory =
specification.
The supported hook names are <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><=
span class=3D"pre">create-symlinks</span></code>,
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">disable-de=
vice-node-modification</span></code>, <code class=3D"docutils literal notra=
nslate"><span class=3D"pre">enable-cuda-compat</span></code>,
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">update-app=
lication-profile</span></code>, and <code class=3D"docutils literal notrans=
late"><span class=3D"pre">update-ldcache</span></code>.
Use <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">all</s=
pan></code> to disable every hook.</p>
<p>The following command disables the update-application-profile and update=
-ldcache
hooks. Separate multiple values with a colon:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell11" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
sudo nvidia-ctk config --in-place <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --set nvidia-container-runtime.modes.jit-cdi.nvcdi-disable-hooks<span c=
lass=3D"o">=3D</span>update-application-profile:update-ldcache
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell11">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>The resulting configuration contains the following settings:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-toml notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell12" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"k">[nvidia-cont=
ainer-runtime.modes.jit-cdi]</span><span class=3D"w"></span>
<span class=3D"n">nvcdi-disable-hooks</span><span class=3D"w"> </span><span=
 class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"p">[</span>=
<span class=3D"s">"update-application-profile"</span><span class=3D"p">,</s=
pan><span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"s">"update-ldcache"</span><spa=
n class=3D"p">]</span><span class=3D"w"></span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell12">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<div class=3D"admonition warning">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Warning</p>
<p>Disable only the hook that conflicts with your environment. Hooks config=
ure
libraries, links, device behavior, and GPU visibility in the container. Dis=
abling
a required hook can prevent an application from starting or can expose more=
 GPUs
to EGL and Vulkan applications than the container requested.</p>
</div>
<p>For a persistent specification, pass <code class=3D"docutils literal not=
ranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--disable-hook</span></code> once for each ho=
ok when you
<a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/=
cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#manual-cdi-specifica=
tion-generation"><span class=3D"std std-doc">generate the CDI specification=
 manually</span></a>:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell13" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
sudo nvidia-ctk cdi generate <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --disable-hook update-application-profile <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --disable-hook update-ldcache <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --output<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>/var/run/cdi/nvidia.yaml
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell13">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"running-a-workload-with-cdi">
<h2>Running a Workload with CDI<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs=
.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.ht=
ml#running-a-workload-with-cdi" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a><=
/h2>
<p>Using CDI to inject NVIDIA devices can conflict with using the NVIDIA Co=
ntainer Runtime hook.
This means that if a <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span cla=
ss=3D"pre">/usr/share/containers/oci/hooks.d/oci-nvidia-hook.json</span></c=
ode> file exists, delete it
or ensure that you do not run containers with the <code class=3D"docutils l=
iteral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span></code=
> environment variable set.</p>
<p>The use of the CDI specification depends on the CDI-enabled container en=
gine or CLI that you use.
In the case of <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"=
pre">podman</span></code>, for example, releases as of <code class=3D"docut=
ils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">v4.1.0</span></code> include s=
upport for specifying CDI devices in the <code class=3D"docutils literal no=
translate"><span class=3D"pre">--device</span></code> argument.
Assuming that you generated a CDI specification as in the preceding section=
, running a container with access to all NVIDIA GPUs requires the following=
 command:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell14" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
podman run --rm --device nvidia.com/gpu<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>all --se=
curity-opt<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"nv">label</span><span =
class=3D"o">=3D</span>disable ubuntu nvidia-smi -L
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell14">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>The preceding sample command should show the same output as running <cod=
e class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-smi</sp=
an> <span class=3D"pre">-L</span></code> on the host.</p>
<p>The CDI specification also contains references to individual GPUs or MIG=
 devices.
You can request these by specifying their names when launching a container,=
 such as the following example:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell15" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
podman run --rm <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --device nvidia.com/gpu<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">0<=
/span> <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --device nvidia.com/gpu<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">1<=
/span>:0 <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    --security-opt<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"nv">label</spa=
n><span class=3D"o">=3D</span>disable <span class=3D"se">\</span>
    ubuntu nvidia-smi -L
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell15">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>The preceding sample command requests the full GPU with index 0 and the =
first MIG device on GPU 1.
The output should show only the UUIDs of the requested devices.</p>
<section id=3D"imex-channels">
<h3>IMEX Channels<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/da=
tacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-support.html#imex-channe=
ls" title=3D"Permalink to this headline">#</a></h3>
<p>Containers can request specific NVIDIA IMEX channels with the
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">NVIDIA_IME=
X_CHANNELS</span></code> environment variable. For supported values, an exa=
mple,
and validation errors, refer to
<a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/=
cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/docker-specialized.html#id1"><span cl=
ass=3D"std std-doc">Requesting IMEX Channels</span></a>.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"using-cdi-with-non-cdi-enabled-runtimes">
<h2>Using CDI with Non-CDI-Enabled Runtimes<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"=
https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cd=
i-support.html#using-cdi-with-non-cdi-enabled-runtimes" title=3D"Permalink =
to this headline">#</a></h2>
<p>To support runtimes that do not natively support CDI, you can configure =
the NVIDIA Container Runtime in a <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">cdi</span></code> mode.
In this mode, the NVIDIA Container Runtime does not inject the NVIDIA Conta=
iner Runtime Hook into the incoming OCI runtime specification.
Instead, the runtime performs the injection of the requested CDI devices.</=
p>
<p>The NVIDIA Container Runtime automatically uses <code class=3D"docutils =
literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">cdi</span></code> mode if you requ=
est devices by their CDI device names.</p>
<p>Using Docker as an example of a non-CDI-enabled runtime, the following c=
ommand uses CDI to inject the requested devices into the container:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell16" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
docker run --rm -ti --runtime<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>nvidia <span class=
=3D"se">\</span>
    -e <span class=3D"nv">NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span><span class=3D"o">=
=3D</span>nvidia.com/gpu<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>all <span class=3D"se">=
\</span>
      ubuntu nvidia-smi -L
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell16">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">NVI=
DIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span></code> environment variable indicates which devi=
ces to inject into the container and is explicitly set to <code class=3D"do=
cutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia.com/gpu=3Dall</span>=
</code>.</p>
<section id=3D"setting-the-cdi-mode-explicitly">
<h3>Setting the CDI Mode Explicitly<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://=
docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/cdi-suppor=
t.html#setting-the-cdi-mode-explicitly" title=3D"Permalink to this headline=
">#</a></h3>
<p>You can force CDI mode by explicitly setting the <code class=3D"docutils=
 literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-container-runtime.mode</sp=
an></code> option in the NVIDIA Container Runtime config to <code class=3D"=
docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">cdi</span></code>:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell17" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
sudo nvidia-ctk config --in-place --set nvidia-container-runtime.mode<span =
class=3D"o">=3D</span>cdi
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell17">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>In this case, the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span cla=
ss=3D"pre">NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span></code> environment variable is sti=
ll used to select the
devices to inject into the container, but the <code class=3D"docutils liter=
al notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">nvidia-container-runtime.modes.cdi.defa=
ult-kind</span></code>
(with a default value of <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span=
 class=3D"pre">nvidia.com/gpu</span></code>) is used to construct a fully-q=
ualified CDI device name
only when you specify a device index such as <code class=3D"docutils litera=
l notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">all</span></code>, <code class=3D"docuti=
ls literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">0</span></code>, or <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">1</span></code>, and =
so on.</p>
<p>This means that if CDI mode is explicitly enabled, the following sample =
command has the same effect as
specifying <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre"=
>NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3Dnvidia.com/gpu=3Dall</span></code>.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell18" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
docker run --rm -ti --runtime<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>nvidia <span class=
=3D"se">\</span>
    -e <span class=3D"nv">NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span><span class=3D"o">=
=3D</span>all <span class=3D"se">\</span>
      ubuntu nvidia-smi -L
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell18">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
